 result←object(State ∆Icon)arg;icon;bits;mask;objname
 ⍝ Create and return an Icon "handle", which contains the name of a new Icon object that can be used later
 ⍝ This handle should be "freed" later with '#' ∆WI '⎕Free'

 ⍝ '?Icon' icon ...

 result←⍬
 :If 1≥|≡arg ⋄ arg←,⊂arg ⋄ :EndIf
 '∆WI RANK ERROR: Icon'##.Error∨/2<≢¨⍴¨arg

 :For icon :In arg
     :If ##.IsInt icon ⍝ This better be an icon handle
     :AndIf 1=≢icon
         result,←⊃icon ⍝ Just return the same pointer intact
     :ElseIf (##.IsChar icon)∧'>'∊icon ⍝ This is an icon resource ⍝? Does this need more thorough validation?
         ##.Error'Icon resources are not supported yet' ⍝? Add this later
     :ElseIf ##.IsChar icon ⍝ This is an icon file name
         '∆WI RANK ERROR: Icon'##.Error 1<≢⍴icon←1/icon
         :If '.ico'≡⍥⎕C ¯4↑icon ⍝ We're only accepting .ICO files ⍝? May do more later
         :AndIf ⎕NEXISTS icon
             objname←(object⍕⍛,'.',##.Next object)##.∆WC'Icon'('File'icon)('Style' 'Large') ⍝ We'll create an object to use later
             ⍝ Build a "handle" namespace pointing to this icon for later reference
             result,←'Icon'CreateHandle(ObjName:objname ⋄ ∆EX:objname) ⍝ Just store the object-reference for later use
         :Else
             ##.Error'∆WI DRAW ERROR: Invalid or missing icon file "',icon,'"'
         :EndIf
     :Else
         ##.Error'∆WI DOMAIN ERROR: Icon'
     :EndIf
 :EndFor
